.TH DANBY-BUDWORM 1
.SH NAME
danby-budworm \- spruce budworm outbreak threshold
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/budworm
.SH MODEL
N' = rN(1-N/K)-BN^2/(A^2+N^2).
.PP
Budworms grow logistically on available foliage.  Bird predation saturates at
high budworm density.  The opposing S-shaped growth and saturating loss curves
can create multiple equilibria, a low endemic state, and a high outbreak state;
parameter changes reveal the threshold and hysteresis directly.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the budworm state bar.  Tracks set intrinsic growth, foliage capacity,
maximum bird predation, and predation saturation.  Space pauses, period steps,
r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/budworm.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/budworm.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR populationmodel (2),
.IR numerics (2)
